## Release safety — mandatory for all AI agents

- This repository has no staging environment. Create `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` branches from `main` and open PRs explicitly into `main`. Do not use `staging`.
- **The only human gate is merging into `main`, which deploys production.** Everything before it (branches, commits, PRs, previews, checks) is agent work and needs no further permission.
- To release, give the PR, its scope, checks and any production steps in one message and wait for one human yes. It covers that PR; ask again only if the PR gains unrelated changes. Merge with a merge commit.
- Never push directly to `main`, bypass protections, or change production outside an approved release.
- Read [RELEASE_POLICY.md](RELEASE_POLICY.md) before release, deployment, environment, schema, or tag work. Verify actual environment destinations before writes.
<!-- END MEAVO RELEASE POLICY -->
